# Context

## Background
This implements Workstream 0 of plans/2026-11-09-upstream-alignment.md,
born from a 145-commit survey of upstream pingdotgg/lawn (fork is 60
ahead / 145 behind, merge-base 046c2b2). Full merge is not viable: 88
conflicts plus three architectural deadlocks (public vs signed playback,
public watch vs team access, version stacks vs per-video grants).

## Why This Way
- Exact pins, not carets: react-start 1.168.60 + react-router 1.170.41
  are upstream's proven pairing. A caret on react-router resolves a
  newer version that nests a second router-core copy into the client
  bundle (caught in adversarial review; verified via sourcemaps).
- @convex-dev/stripe 0.1.4 exact: a caret drifts to 0.1.7 which pulls
  stripe ^22 alongside our direct stripe ^20 - two SDK copies.
- CVE-2026-102989 (GHSA-qx66-fv34-fjm8) is an app-wide server-function
  transport XSS, not a public-route issue; Vercel already refuses
  builds resolving react-start 1.160.2.
- Presence hardening (upstream 8d641f9) was NOT ported: our query
  derives videos server-side, so the crash class never existed. The
  new comment on listProjectOnlineCounts guards the invariant.

## Gotchas
- No code may construct stream.mux.com URLs: client never does; server
  builders require a token at compile time. seo.ts preconnects and test
  fixtures are the only permitted references.
- Local `bun run build` fails at prerender on clean HEAD too
  (environmental; needs deploy env). Validate locally with typecheck,
  lint, and tests; bundle compilation succeeds before prerender.

